ng that work remains possible or access recovers\"}]}, \"LOW\": {\"definition\": \"Localized issue that appears to have limited impact on labeling quality or workflow. The available context suggests a minor inconvenience or straightforward correction rather than a substantive operational problem.\", \"examples\": \"One-off clarification of otherwise clear guidance; minor LT inconvenience; isolated inconsistency with little downstream impact; a confusing FAQ heading when the underlying rule is understood and usable.\", \"signals\": []}, \"N/A\": {\"definition\": \"No identifiable operational problem or risk requiring severity assessment. Includes casual chat, pure social threads, and routine announcements.\", \"examples\": \"Routine announcements, informational updates, acknowledgments, administrative messages, general discussion without an actionable issue.\", \"signals\": []}, \"UNKNOWN\": {\"definition\": \"The report and available context are too ambiguous or incomplete to meaningfully assess operational impact. Missing explicit impact wording, affected-task counts, or a confirmed technical cause does not by itself require UNKNOWN.\", \"examples\": \"'Something looks wrong' without describing the behavior; a report referring to missing context; contradictory accounts that leave it unclear whether there is a minor display issue or an inability to complete the task.\", \"signals\": []}}}, \"limits\": {\"follow_up_queries\": 3}, \"previous_draft\": {\"contract_version\": \"agent3-advisor-draft-v11\", \"summary\": \"A QA tutor reports that some QA reviewers count light clipping as major. Current guidance judges clipping by its effect on speech intelligibility; an earlier approved focused review has no recorded booking or outcome in the retrieved decision.\", \"summary_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that some QA reviewers count light clipping as major.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\"], \"depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"Current guidance judges clipping by its effect on speech intelligibility; an earlier approved focused review has no recorded booking or outcome in the retrieved decision.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c2\", \"c4\"], \"depends_on\": []}], \"detail_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"The earlier review record describes one example with a short pop and every word intelligible, and another with repeated distortion and disagreement over recoverable words.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c5\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"The earlier decision preserved the brief, intelligible minor example and held any new threshold until the disputed recording was reviewed.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c4\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}], \"reasoning\": \"The QA tutor's report raises a scoring-consistency concern, but it does not establish that any particular rating was wrong: the report supplies no affected span or intelligibility assessment. The current instructions and FAQ agree on handling. The earlier decision supports a focused review rather than a new duration-based rule, but scheduling and outcome research is needed before arranging another session.\", \"claims\": [{\"claim_id\": \"c1\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that some QA reviewers count light clipping as major.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790860406.000119\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790860406.000119\"}], \"quote\": \"Some QA count light clipping as major.\", \"quote_kind\": \"VERBATIM\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c2\", \"kind\": \"GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions make brief, localized clipping with clear speech minor and an artifact making a material speech span unusable major; continuous artifacts or borderline impact require QA review with timestamps and an intelligibility description, and duration alone does not establish a major defect.\", \"evidence_ids\": [